WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
Baghdad, 1095.

2
00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:07.220
A leading teacher publishes a book
attacking the philosophers of his day.

3
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.310
His name is al-Ghazali.

4
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.930
He says some of their ideas go
beyond error, into unbelief.

5
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.530
Decades later in Cordoba, a judge
named Ibn Rushd answered him.

6
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.890
So can a believer follow
reason all the way,

7
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.800
or does knowing God need more than reason?

8
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:29.710
In this mission, you'll see the three charges
al-Ghazali brought against the philosophers.

9
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.330
Then you'll hear how Ibn
Rushd defended philosophy.

10
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.880
Your mission: weigh up whether a
believer can follow reason all the way,

11
00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.200
or needs more than reason to know God.
